<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Comprehensive Anti-Apartheid Act</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1986</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Comprehensive Anti-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apartheid">Apartheid</a> Act was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> law of 1986 that imposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanctions">sanctions</a> on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>, banning new investment, bank loans and imports of goods such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coal">coal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/steel">steel</a> and uranium, and ending direct air links. Congress passed it over the veto of President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ronald-reagan">Ronald Reagan</a>, and it set conditions for lifting the sanctions, including the release of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nelson-mandela">Nelson Mandela</a>.</p></div>
